Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a practical reliability strategy for multi-tenant, geo-distributed services under sudden load, balancing fairness and SLA adherence.

Key Concepts

- QoS with quotas and burst budgets
- Ingress-level enforcement and sidecar orchestration
- Dynamic rate limiting and circuit breakers
- Cross-region traffic steering and graceful degradation
- Observability: SLI/SLO dashboards, latency tails, queue depth
- Rollout/rollback: staged changes, synthetic tests, rapid revert

Code Example

```javascript
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(capacity, fillRate) {
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.fillRate = fillRate; // tokens per second
    this.last = Date.now();
  }
  allow(n = 1) {
    this._inject();
    if (this.tokens >= n) { this.tokens -= n; return true; }
    return false;
  }
  _inject() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.last) / 1000;
    this.last = now;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + elapsed * this.fillRate);
  }
}
```

Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure and trigger a regional SLA breach, and what would your kill-switch look like?
- What data would you surface in dashboards to operators during a flash spike?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical SRE skills: incident triage, region-aware rollouts, backpressure, circuit breaking, and rollback discipline beyond basic incident response.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-region latency analysis
- Cache stampede mitigation
- Per-region deployment strategies (canary, rollouts)
- Safe rollback criteria and instrumentation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple circuit breaker (pseudo)
class CircuitBreaker {
  constructor(threshold) { this.open = false; this.failures = 0; this.threshold = threshold; }
  onFailure() { this.failures++; if (this.failures > this.threshold) this.open = true; }
  allow() { return !this.open; }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this to a service mesh with traffic shifting?
- How would you verify rollback correctness across all regions post-incident?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical mastery of deduplication in real systems, combining transactional patterns, Kafka exactly-once semantics, and robust auditing.

## Key Concepts

- Exactly-once processing
- Transactional outbox pattern
- Kafka transactions (transactional.id)
- Idempotency keys and dedupe stores
- Compensating actions and audit trails

